    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nnew\n\n### Description\n\n### Feature Request: Automatic Virtual Environment Selection (for Python/Conda)\n\n**Description:**\n\nI would like to request a new plugin or feature for the mini.nvim series that automatically selects and activates the appropriate virtual environment, such as Python environments (including Conda). This would streamline the process of working with different Python projects and virtual environments in Neovim.\n\n**Proposed Features:**\n- Automatically detect the virtual environment based on the project \n\n> directory (e.g., `env` or `venv` folders, `.conda` environments).\n\n- Support for detecting and switching Conda environments.\n- Option to define a custom path for virtual environments.\n- Option to manually activate or deactivate environments.\n- Automatic activation upon opening Python files or projects.\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Saves time by automatically handling virtual environments.\n- Reduces the need for manual environment management.\n- Ensures that the correct dependencies are used for each project.\n- Enhances workflow, especially for Python/Conda users in Neovim.\n\n**Additional Information:**\n- The plugin could be built to interface with existing Python/Conda management tools like `pyenv`, `conda`, or `virtualenv`.\n- Could provide simple commands to switch between environments if needed.\n\n**Thank you for considering this feature!**",
